  "lean": {
    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    (μ : Measure E) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ] {η : ℝ} (hη : 0 < η)\n    {f : E → ℝ} (hf : ContDiff ℝ 1 f) (hc : HasCompactSupport f) :\n    let R := fun y : E => μ.tilted (fun x => -‖x-y‖^2/(2*η))\n    let S := fun y : E => (R y).map (fun x : E => (2:ℝ) • x-y)\n    ContDiff ℝ 1 (fun y : E => ∫ u, f u ∂S y)",
    "statement_sha256": "7245b6c8d63e3ba7a39b2b8b9b414b666324c9339a177d60ef87f675acebc97c",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its norm and Borel measurable structure, including rank zero. μ is any probability measure, η is a positive real number, and f is a globally continuously Frechet differentiable real function with compact support. No moment, density, domination, normalizer or derivative-continuity certificate is a hypothesis.",
      "Measure.tilted means the actual exponentially tilted measure: for real likelihood log-weight q, μ.tilted(q) has density exp(q)/integral exp(q) dμ against μ whenever this weight is integrable. The specified quadratic Gaussian weight is used literally at every y, not only almost everywhere.",
      "R(y) is exactly the displayed quadratic tilt of μ with variance parameter η. S(y) is the actual measurable pushforward of R(y) by the affine reflection x ↦ 2x-y. No arbitrary conditional-kernel version is substituted.",
      "The integral is the real Bochner expectation of f under this S(y). ContDiff ℝ 1 means global C1 regularity in y of that exact mean, with actual continuous Frechet derivative. HasCompactSupport refers to compact closure of the nonzero support.",
      "This statement asserts only regularity of the compact-observer mean. It provides no rough-observer gradient domain, curvature/energy constant, mixing, implementable sampler or expected-query-cost conclusion."
    ]
  },
